1
00:02:45,247 --> 00:02:47,409
<v ANGELA> Hello, Flanders conference hotel.

2
00:02:47,677 --> 00:02:54,628
<v MAN> Oh, hi. I wanted to ask about conference facilities at the hotel. Have I come through to the right person?

3
00:02:54,628 --> 00:03:01,612
<v ANGELA> You have. I’m the customer services manager. My name’s Angela. So how can I help you?

4
00:03:01,707 --> 00:03:07,035
<v MAN> Well, I’m calling from Barrett and Stansons, we’re a medical company based in Perth.

5
00:03:07,035 --> 00:03:07,987
<v ANGELA> Oh yes.

6
00:03:08,277 --> 00:03:17,733
<v MAN> And we’re organising a conference for our clients to be held in Sydney. It’ll be held over two days and we’re expecting about fifty or sixty people.

7
00:03:17,893 --> 00:03:19,535
<v ANGELA> When were you thinking of having it?

8
00:03:19,838 --> 00:03:25,658
<v MAN> Some time early next year, like the end of January? It’d have to be a weekend.

9
00:03:25,812 --> 00:03:38,533
<v ANGELA> Let me see … our conference facilities are already booked for the weekend beginning January 28th. We could do the first weekend in February?

10
00:03:38,654 --> 00:03:41,498
<v MAN> How about January 21st?

11
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:45,369
<v ANGELA> I’m afraid that’s booked too.

12
00:03:45,588 --> 00:03:48,455
<v MAN> Well, let’s go for the February date then.

13
00:03:48,579 --> 00:03:52,441
<v ANGELA> So that’s the weekend beginning the 4th.

14
00:03:52,562 --> 00:03:58,274
<v MAN> OK. Now can you tell me a bit about what conference facilities you have?

15
00:03:58,457 --> 00:04:04,556
<v ANGELA> Sure. So for talks and presentations we have the Tesla room.

16
00:04:04,694 --> 00:04:05,436
<v MAN> Sorry?

17
00:04:05,532 --> 00:04:18,314
<v ANGELA> Tesla – that’s spelled T-E-S-L-A. it holds up to a hundred people, and it’s fully equipped with a projector and so on.

18
00:04:18,431 --> 00:04:19,855
<v MAN> How about a microphone?

19
00:04:19,990 --> 00:04:28,877
<v ANGELA> Yes, that’ll be all set up ready for you, and there’ll be one that members of the audience can use too, for questions, if necessary.

20
00:04:29,002 --> 00:04:43,854
<v MAN> Fine. And we’ll also need some sort of open area where people can sit and have a cup of coffee, and we’d like to have an exhibition of our products and services there as well, so that’ll need to be quite a big space.

21
00:04:43,966 --> 00:04:54,570
<v ANGELA> That’s fine, there’s a central atrium with all those facilities, and you can come before the conference starts if you want to set everything up.

22
00:04:54,678 --> 00:04:58,185
<v MAN> Great. And I presume there’s wifi?

23
00:04:58,308 --> 00:05:03,123
<v ANGELA> Oh yes, that’s free and available throughout the hotel.

24
00:05:03,239 --> 00:05:04,273
<v MAN> OK.

25
00:05:04,401 --> 00:05:11,895
<v ANGELA> Would you also like us to provide a buffet lunch? We can do a two-course meal with a number of different options.

26
00:05:12,083 --> 00:05:14,476
<v MAN> What sort of price are we looking at for that?

27
00:05:14,598 --> 00:05:26,553
<v ANGELA> Well, I can send you a copy of the standard menu. That’s $45 per person. Or you can have the special for $25 more.

28
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:31,610
<v MAN> I think the standard should be OK, but yes, send me the menu.

29
00:06:13,662 --> 00:06:25,730
<v MAN> Now we’re also going to need accommodation on the Saturday night for some of the participants … I’m not sure how many, but probably about 25. So what do you change for a room?

30
00:06:25,876 --> 00:06:39,988
<v ANGELA> Well, for conference attendees we have a 25% reduction, so we can offer you rooms at $135. Normally a standard room’s $180.

31
00:06:40,113 --> 00:06:42,067
<v MAN> And does that include breakfast?

32
00:06:42,067 --> 00:06:58,213
<v ANGELA> Sure. And of course, guests can also make use of all the other facilities at the hotel. So we’ve got a spa where you can get massages and facials and so on, and there’s a pool up on the roof for the use of guests.

33
00:06:58,339 --> 00:07:05,084
<v MAN> Great. Now what about transport links? The hotel’s downtown, isn’t it?

34
00:07:05,213 --> 00:07:16,958
<v ANGELA> Yes, it’s about 12 kilometres from the airport, but there’s a complimentary shuttle bus for guests. And it’s only about ten minutes’ walk from the central railway station.

35
00:07:17,093 --> 00:07:24,029
<v MAN> OK. Now, I don’t know Sydney very well, can you just give me an idea of the location of the hotel?

36
00:07:24,179 --> 00:07:50,860
<v ANGELA> Well, it’s downtown on Wilby Street, that’s quite a small street, and it’s not very far from the sea. And of course if the conference attendees want to go out on the Saturday evening there’s a huge choice of places to eat. Then if they want to make a night of it, they can go on to one of the clubs in the area – there are a great many to choose from.

37
00:07:51,047 --> 00:07:58,983
<v MAN> OK. So if we go ahead with this, can you give me some information about how much …